{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 6,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.629,
            0.065,
            0.833,
            0.081
          ],
          "content": "Patterns in Mathematics"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.121,
            0.437,
            0.141
          ],
          "content": "Here is how it can be done:"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.353,
            0.154,
            0.594,
            0.336
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_6_image_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.346,
            0.527,
            0.368
          ],
          "content": "This picture now makes it evident that"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.34,
            0.38,
            0.608,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": "1+3+5+7+9+11=36.",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.412,
            0.833,
            0.457
          ],
          "content": "Because such a picture can be made for a square of any size, this explains why adding up odd numbers gives square numbers."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.461,
            0.833,
            0.506
          ],
          "content": "By drawing a similar picture, can you say what is the sum of the first 10 odd numbers?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.51,
            0.833,
            0.556
          ],
          "content": "Now by imagining a similar picture, or by drawing it partially, as needed, can you say what is the sum of the first 100 odd numbers?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.569,
            0.744,
            0.614
          ],
          "content": "**Another example of such a relation between sequences: Adding up and down**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.619,
            0.498,
            0.64
          ],
          "content": "Let us look at the following pattern:"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.971,
            0.549,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.239,
            0.649,
            0.296,
            0.669
          ],
          "content": "1 = 1",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.239,
            0.672,
            0.371,
            0.691
          ],
          "content": "1+2+1=4",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.24,
            0.694,
            0.442,
            0.714
          ],
          "content": "1+2+3+2+1=9",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.24,
            0.717,
            0.527,
            0.737
          ],
          "content": "1+2+3+4+3+2+1=16",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.24,
            0.74,
            0.599,
            0.76
          ],
          "content": "1+2+3+4+5+4+3+2+1=25",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.241,
            0.762,
            0.671,
            0.782
          ],
          "content": "1+2+3+4+5+6+5+4+3+2+1=36",
          "image_source": "images/page_6_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.813,
            0.833,
            0.859
          ],
          "content": "This seems to be giving yet another way of getting the square numbers— by adding the counting numbers up and then down!"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.891,
            0.944,
            0.91,
            0.96
          ],
          "content": "7"
        }
      ]
    }
